<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Aries half year EPS, div rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Aries half year EPS, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		16.1	  vs 11.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 4.0	   vs 3.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1.78	  vs 1.21</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.82	  vs 1.94</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.04	  vs 0.73</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.29	  vs 0.19</p>
<p>    Turnover		  22.72	 vs 19.19</p>
<p>Insurance claim proceeds</p>
<p>				  0.79	  vs nil</p>
<p>Div payable September 19</p>
<p>on register August 22</p>
<p>Full name: Aries Packaging Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that following a half year of competitive business conditions, no improvement in the general environment was foreseen, except that seasonally the second half of the year was better than the first.</p>
<p>The firm was, however, in a very stable financial position and actively looking for suitable acquisitions. Certain modernisation of its existing machinery is also at an advanced stage and should result in improved results for the full year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
